2026-11-06T03:09:02.4950979Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4959377Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4960017Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4960467Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4960754Z 
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4960991Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4961281Z 
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4961540Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4962076Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4962299Z 
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4962431Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4962732Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4962967Z 
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4963206Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:09:02.4963662Z   $ sh ./install-nix
